\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Hardy had his reasons too. A state government department had bought the quarry the foyer marble had been hacked from and was using it for public schools and crisis centres.\
Never one to miss an opportunity to make whole subterranean floors disappear while doing his civic duty and protesting that a government should\'97
\f2\i Markets forbid!
\f1\i0 \'97own anything, Hardy ordered the works to begin. No one noticed the lift well round the back of the lift hall being filled with concrete during the first two days of remodelling, which went on for some weeks. The quantity amused Hardy: 6,024 cubic metres. It reminded him of his favourite verse from the New Ulyssian Market Bible\'97Cashiers 6:24: 
\f2\i You shall serve both God and money. 
\f1\i0 No contractor asked who or what was down there; it was the weekend and they were being paid triple time.\
The foyer reopened a week earlier than planned. No one noticed there was one less set of lift doors, though everyone praised the new marble fa\'e7ades.\
Hardy received the news via text message and thought no more of it, satisfied he had prevented something considerably worse than disease.
